1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,765
Mastery evidence.

2
00:00:01,765 --> 00:00:04,889
You have learned Python for DevOps: setup,

3
00:00:04,889 --> 00:00:05,708
data types,

4
00:00:05,708 --> 00:00:06,154
files,

5
00:00:06,154 --> 00:00:07,047
REST A P Is,

6
00:00:07,047 --> 00:00:07,865
exceptions,

7
00:00:07,865 --> 00:00:09,279
command line tools,

8
00:00:09,279 --> 00:00:09,725
tests,

9
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:10,990
and cloud S D Ks.

10
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:12,255
Now you prove it.

11
00:00:12,805 --> 00:00:15,626
Mastery means someone else could check your work.

12
00:00:15,626 --> 00:00:17,412
So this lesson gives you a lab,

13
00:00:17,412 --> 00:00:19,312
a checker that says pass or fail,

14
00:00:19,312 --> 00:00:21,615
and a report that shows how you thought.

15
00:00:22,165 --> 00:00:26,965
I will build the lab, fix the first broken script live, and leave the other three to you.

16
00:00:29,015 --> 00:00:33,836
Meet a small team's toolbox. Four Python scripts, each one broken on purpose.

17
00:00:34,386 --> 00:00:37,074
A checker prints pass or fail for four checks.

18
00:00:37,624 --> 00:00:41,571
One: top dot P Y must sort ports as numbers, not as text.

19
00:00:42,121 --> 00:00:47,055
Two: load config dot P Y must print a clear error and exit with code two,

20
00:00:47,055 --> 00:00:48,542
not dump a trace back.

21
00:00:49,092 --> 00:00:53,338
Three: fetch dot P Y must exit with code one when it gives up.

22
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:57,557
Four: tags dot P Y must give every call a fresh list.

23
00:00:58,107 --> 00:01:01,456
Your mission: four pass lines, with proof for every fix.

24
00:01:03,506 --> 00:01:07,709
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

25
00:01:08,259 --> 00:01:13,933
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

26
00:01:14,483 --> 00:01:17,483
The lab is one file: lab fifty-six dot S H,

27
00:01:17,483 --> 00:01:19,715
in the academy slash lab folder.

28
00:01:19,715 --> 00:01:25,086
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson fifty-six.

29
00:01:25,636 --> 00:01:27,517
Install it in three steps.

30
00:01:27,517 --> 00:01:29,036
Clone the repository.

31
00:01:29,036 --> 00:01:30,555
Go to the lab folder.

32
00:01:30,555 --> 00:01:34,895
Install the script into slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

33
00:01:35,445 --> 00:01:37,466
Three commands run everything.

34
00:01:37,466 --> 00:01:39,285
Lab up builds the problems.

35
00:01:39,285 --> 00:01:41,913
Lab check prints pass or fail for each.

36
00:01:41,913 --> 00:01:43,530
Lab down removes it all.

37
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,481
Lab is a short name.

38
00:01:45,481 --> 00:01:47,303
Source the shortcuts file,

39
00:01:47,303 --> 00:01:48,634
and it runs sue do,

40
00:01:48,634 --> 00:01:50,175
lab fifty-six dot S H,

41
00:01:50,175 --> 00:01:50,736
for you.

42
00:01:51,286 --> 00:01:55,151
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root and python three,

43
00:01:55,151 --> 00:01:56,523
which Ubuntu includes.

44
00:01:56,523 --> 00:01:58,518
Run it only in your own machine.

45
00:02:00,868 --> 00:02:01,800
Now for real.

46
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,879
I have cloned the repository,

47
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:07,104
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

48
00:02:07,104 --> 00:02:07,749
Type: CD,

49
00:02:07,749 --> 00:02:08,036
lab.

50
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:10,741
List what is here. Type: L S.

51
00:02:11,291 --> 00:02:14,349
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

52
00:02:14,349 --> 00:02:15,878
Install the script.

53
00:02:15,878 --> 00:02:16,924
Type: sue do,

54
00:02:16,924 --> 00:02:17,568
install,

55
00:02:17,568 --> 00:02:18,131
dash m,

56
00:02:18,131 --> 00:02:19,419
seven five five,

57
00:02:19,419 --> 00:02:21,189
lab fifty-six dot S H,

58
00:02:21,189 --> 00:02:24,086
slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

59
00:02:24,086 --> 00:02:27,547
Dash m seven five five makes it executable.

60
00:02:28,097 --> 00:02:32,769
Load the short names. Type: source, shortcuts fifty-six dot S H.

61
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:35,345
Build the lab. Type: lab up.

62
00:02:37,895 --> 00:02:40,477
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

63
00:02:42,027 --> 00:02:46,187
Four FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

64
00:02:48,237 --> 00:02:49,986
Keep four notes for every fault.

65
00:02:50,536 --> 00:02:55,080
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the error, or the exact wrong output.

66
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:58,062
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

67
00:02:58,612 --> 00:03:00,895
Three: the fix. One change only.

68
00:03:01,445 --> 00:03:03,877
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

69
00:03:04,427 --> 00:03:06,582
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

70
00:03:08,632 --> 00:03:09,391
Fault one,

71
00:03:09,391 --> 00:03:09,770
live.

72
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:14,323
The checker says top dot P Y does not sort ports as numbers.

73
00:03:14,323 --> 00:03:16,220
Go to the scripts folder.

74
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:16,903
Type: CD,

75
00:03:16,903 --> 00:03:17,662
slash opt,

76
00:03:17,662 --> 00:03:19,180
slash lab fifty-six,

77
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:19,939
slash bin.

78
00:03:20,489 --> 00:03:23,125
Run the script the way the checker does,

79
00:03:23,125 --> 00:03:25,102
with three ports out of order.

80
00:03:25,102 --> 00:03:26,354
Type: python three,

81
00:03:26,354 --> 00:03:27,145
top dot P Y,

82
00:03:27,145 --> 00:03:27,606
eighty,

83
00:03:27,606 --> 00:03:28,660
four four three,

84
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,110
eight zero eight zero.

85
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,240
Note one,

86
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:34,400
the symptom: four four three comes before eighty.

87
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,077
That is not numeric order.

88
00:03:36,077 --> 00:03:38,012
Now find the cause with proof,

89
00:03:38,012 --> 00:03:38,850
do not guess.

90
00:03:38,850 --> 00:03:42,719
Ask Python how it sorts the text eighty and four four three.

91
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:43,945
Type: python three,

92
00:03:43,945 --> 00:03:44,396
dash C,

93
00:03:44,396 --> 00:03:45,815
and a print of sorted,

94
00:03:45,815 --> 00:03:47,556
with the two ports as text.

95
00:03:48,106 --> 00:03:48,700
Note two,

96
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:49,360
the cause.

97
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,670
Text sorts one character at a time,

98
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:54,443
and the character four comes before eight.

99
00:03:54,443 --> 00:03:57,611
Arguments from the command line are always text.

100
00:03:57,611 --> 00:03:58,337
Note three,

101
00:03:58,337 --> 00:04:00,780
one change: sort with int as the key.

102
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,440
Type: sed,

103
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:01,902
dash i,

104
00:04:01,902 --> 00:04:04,938
and the substitution that adds key equals int.

105
00:04:05,488 --> 00:04:06,193
Note four,

106
00:04:06,193 --> 00:04:06,899
the proof.

107
00:04:06,899 --> 00:04:09,580
Run it again with the very same ports.

108
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:10,920
Type: python three,

109
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:11,767
top dot P Y,

110
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:13,531
and the same three ports.

111
00:04:14,281 --> 00:04:14,758
Eighty,

112
00:04:14,758 --> 00:04:15,848
four four three,

113
00:04:15,848 --> 00:04:17,347
eight zero eight zero.

114
00:04:17,347 --> 00:04:18,505
In numeric order.

115
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:19,868
Now ask the checker.

116
00:04:19,868 --> 00:04:20,958
Type: lab check.

117
00:04:21,508 --> 00:04:22,094
One PASS,

118
00:04:22,094 --> 00:04:22,810
three FAIL.

119
00:04:22,810 --> 00:04:23,786
One fault down,

120
00:04:23,786 --> 00:04:24,503
one change,

121
00:04:24,503 --> 00:04:25,219
with proof.

122
00:04:25,219 --> 00:04:27,823
Now it is your turn for the other three.

123
00:04:29,873 --> 00:04:33,649
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

124
00:04:34,199 --> 00:04:36,332
Setup: the checker output at the start.

125
00:04:36,882 --> 00:04:38,504
Each fault, with its four notes.

126
00:04:39,054 --> 00:04:42,211
The final checker output, all four lines saying pass.

127
00:04:42,761 --> 00:04:43,889
Where you got stuck,

128
00:04:43,889 --> 00:04:45,074
and what unstuck you.

129
00:04:45,074 --> 00:04:47,838
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

130
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:50,458
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

131
00:04:52,408 --> 00:04:55,459
Your three faults. No spoilers, only directions.

132
00:04:56,009 --> 00:05:01,416
Check two: load config dot P Y crashes with a trace back when the key port is missing.

133
00:05:01,416 --> 00:05:01,856
Run it,

134
00:05:01,856 --> 00:05:04,182
read the last line of the trace back,

135
00:05:04,182 --> 00:05:06,697
and then ask what exit code it returned.

136
00:05:06,697 --> 00:05:08,080
Which exception is it,

137
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,281
and how do you catch only that one?

138
00:05:10,831 --> 00:05:13,770
Check three: fetch dot P Y tries three times,

139
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:14,750
prints gave up,

140
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:16,449
and still exits with zero.

141
00:05:16,449 --> 00:05:20,107
A script that gives up has to say so with its exit code.

142
00:05:20,107 --> 00:05:21,348
Which call sets it?

143
00:05:21,898 --> 00:05:23,793
Check four: run tags dot P Y.

144
00:05:23,793 --> 00:05:26,145
The second list contains both items.

145
00:05:26,145 --> 00:05:28,432
A default argument is created once,

146
00:05:28,432 --> 00:05:30,327
when the function is defined.

147
00:05:30,327 --> 00:05:31,960
What is the safe default,

148
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:34,378
and where does the new list get made?

149
00:05:34,928 --> 00:05:37,031
Same method every time: symptom,

150
00:05:37,031 --> 00:05:37,425
check,

151
00:05:37,425 --> 00:05:38,345
fix one thing,

152
00:05:38,345 --> 00:05:38,805
verify.

153
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,499
And read a trace back from the bottom up.

154
00:05:43,549 --> 00:05:46,941
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

155
00:05:48,491 --> 00:05:54,038
Proof one: is the lab folder gone? Type: L S, slash opt, slash lab fifty-six.

156
00:05:54,588 --> 00:05:56,678
No such file or directory.

157
00:05:56,678 --> 00:05:58,849
Proof two: count it in opt.

158
00:05:58,849 --> 00:05:59,654
Type: L S,

159
00:05:59,654 --> 00:06:00,458
slash opt,

160
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:00,860
pipe,

161
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,825
grep dash c,

162
00:06:01,825 --> 00:06:02,950
lab fifty-six.

163
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:03,932
Zero.

164
00:06:03,932 --> 00:06:06,784
Now remove the lab script itself.

165
00:06:06,784 --> 00:06:07,907
Type: sue do,

166
00:06:07,907 --> 00:06:08,253
R M,

167
00:06:08,253 --> 00:06:13,783
slash U S R slash local slash S bin slash lab fifty-six dot S H.

168
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:17,529
Proof three: is anything left in S bin?

169
00:06:17,529 --> 00:06:18,349
Type: L S,

170
00:06:18,349 --> 00:06:21,299
slash U S R slash local slash S bin,

171
00:06:21,299 --> 00:06:21,709
pipe,

172
00:06:21,709 --> 00:06:22,037
W C,

173
00:06:22,037 --> 00:06:22,610
dash l.

174
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:27,128
Zero. Everything is removed. Paste these proofs into your report.

175
00:06:29,178 --> 00:06:33,103
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

176
00:06:33,653 --> 00:06:35,488
The checker shows four pass lines.

177
00:06:36,038 --> 00:06:39,238
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

178
00:06:39,788 --> 00:06:41,537
You changed one thing at a time.

179
00:06:42,087 --> 00:06:44,903
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

180
00:06:45,453 --> 00:06:47,800
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind.

181
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:50,739
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

182
00:06:51,289 --> 00:06:52,911
To pass, you need all six.

183
00:06:54,961 --> 00:07:00,828
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

184
00:07:01,378 --> 00:07:04,151
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

185
00:07:04,701 --> 00:07:07,517
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

186
00:07:08,067 --> 00:07:11,288
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

187
00:07:11,838 --> 00:07:13,950
Four: write the report from the template.

188
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,679
Five: run the checker. All four lines must say pass.

189
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:20,192
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

190
00:07:20,742 --> 00:07:22,576
Pause the video, and begin now.

191
00:07:38,126 --> 00:07:39,001
Quick check.

192
00:07:39,551 --> 00:07:42,537
Why does text sorting put four four three before eighty?

193
00:07:43,087 --> 00:07:45,967
Which exit code did we use for a bad config file?

194
00:07:46,517 --> 00:07:49,461
Why is an empty list a risky default argument?

195
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:51,569
What proves your cleanup worked?

196
00:07:52,119 --> 00:07:54,989
Mastery evidence covered: M C zero six,

197
00:07:54,989 --> 00:07:57,566
building on objectives one to nine,

198
00:07:57,566 --> 00:08:00,289
in the Python for DevOps masterclass.

199
